ty matters  glenn where is the accountability for  those individuals who push these  lockdowns  of kids that went on in some cases for  almost two years shut them out of  schools drove suicide drug abuse  despondency despair  that was called disinformation a couple  of years ago now it's called  truth  so who gets to decide all that  this is the the critical part where i  mean listening to that it that is  actually incredibly menacing incredibly  insidious to have the attorney general  essentially saying  directing private companies twitter  facebook google telling them you are not  allowed to  air this kind of information that we  regard as hateful or we regard as gain  that is not the government's role to be  arbitrating our political debates by  instructing private companies what they  can and can't do and this has always  been the most misunderstood and over  most overlooked component of this big  tech censorship which is you know  democrats always say if you complain  about you know bias censorship oh well  these are private companies they can do  what they want i never knew democrats  thought about private enterprise that  way that the government has no role to  restrict them but the reality is the  whole time the democrats have been  threatening big tech in exactly the way  you just heard if you don't censor in  accordance with what we want we are  going to impose regulatory and legal  reprisals on you this is coming from the  government and not really emanating from  big tech yeah whether it was the surgeon  general or the attorney general or the  head of dhs or some you know dippy woman  in charge of the disinformation board  it's still sending a a chilling message  and a message of intimidation to critics  of various government policies you  cannot get away from that and glenn  there was um  a pretty sparsely covered  house hearing that it took place a  couple of days ago and  uh a professor that the biden dhs  is giving over  like a half a million dollars to  he exchanged in this interesting  conversation with congressman dan bishop  watch  stochastic terrorism you describe it as  quote a form of incited terrorism  whereby a communicator has access to a  platform and big audience you also say  that with respect to the 2019 el paso  walmart mass shooting  of people of hispanic descent that  president trump was a stochastic  terrorist of that event right correct  among others yes  okay it all relates to data and  collecting data as to whether one  connects to the other and that's the  research i'm trying to conduct now  so glenn now the professoriate  uh is in on the game as well  yeah what they're doing is promulgating  theories that have been long used by  censors to justify  censorship over the internet so let's  imagine that you probably recall three  years ago somebody went to a softball  field where republican congressmen  congregate to play softball and shot as  many as they could almost killing steve  scalise it turned out he was a very  fanatical fan of the rachel maddow show  he loved bernie sanders you could use  that same theory we just heard to say oh  well they're insightful terrorists they  lead people to do violence or the person  who just got arrested outside brett  kavanaugh's house attempting to murder  him because he didn't like the way he  was going to vote on roe and gun control  and you can say who radicalized him  these are terrorists these are the worst  and most dangerous theories that have  long been debunked and discredited to  say any information that i want censored  it's not really speech it's terrorism  it's disinformation it's hate speech  it's all the same thing which is an  attempt to prevent us from having the  right of free speech the constitution  guarantees  glenn great to see you as always hey  sean hannity here hey click here to  subscribe to fox news youtube page and  catch our hottest interviews and most  compelling analysis you will not get it  anywhere else

